. २७; Vi. I. १०. ११; II. १०. २२.
advised Citraratha, who fell to the ground to gather कौशिक's bones to throw them into the सरस्वती and get redemption;
2: भा.

. ४०.
They go in front of the Sun from his rise to his setting, singing his glory;
3: Ib. XII. ११. ४९; Br. II. ११. ३७; २१. ११५; २३. २८ and ४९, M. १२६. २८; वा. 2. २७; २३. १५९; २८. ३१; ५०. १६८; ५२. २६ and ४९; ५४. 8; ५५. ४१; ५९. ९१.
live on air; sages by तपस्; authors of certain सम्हितस्; live in Brahmaloka;
4: Br. II. २५. 4; २६. ४३; ३२. ९९; ३५. ७१ and ९४;

(I)--originally born out of an ant-hill, born again of चर्षणी and वरुण. In his आश्रम, शीता was left when pregnant. There she gave birth to two sons whom the sage brought up;
1: भा. VI. १८. 5; IX. ११. १०-11, १५; Br. III. ३६. 6.
author of राम's story; of the family of भार्गव;
2: M. १२. ५१.
heard it from नारद who got it from ब्रह्मा.
3: Ib. ५३. ७१-2.
वेदव्यास of the २६थ् dva1para;
4: Vi.
